  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1955\n£10.00\n\nLow stock, 5 remaining\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1955 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O., D.L. Volume LVII January to December 1955.\n\nPublished 1956 - The Alden Press (Oxford) Ltd. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' 1955 -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed on December 31st, 1955 -p.6\n\nFormer Officers of the Regiment on the Active List December 31st, 1955 -p.7\n\nGeneral Sir Bernard Paget, G.C.B., D.S.O., M.C. -p.8\n\nRecords of the First Battallion -p.10\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary 1955 -p.13\n\nFirst Battalion Letter -p.21\n\nFirst Battalion Records of Sport and Training 1955 -p.27\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters -p.44\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.45\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion -p.48\n\nFourth Battalion Letter -p.52\n\nThe Laying-Up of the Old Colours of the Fourth Battalion (T.A.) -p.54\n\nRegimental Dinner 1955 -p.55\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner 1955 -p.56\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon 1955 -p.57\n\nThe Bicentenary Celebrations of the 52nd Light Infantry at Osnabruck -p.58\n\nA Week-End at Osnabruck -p.76\n\nCan We Win? -p.79\n\nRandom Reflections on Retirement -p.84\n\nLife in the Rhineland -p.90\n\nMercer Tod Letters -p.96\n\nColonels of the Regiment -p.101\n\nLieut.-General Sir Robert Garrett -p.103\n\nGliding -p.106\n\nAn Outer Island -p.113\n\nCooks Tour - Germany and Switzerland -p.117\n\n Guests at the Castle -p.121\n\nOld Comrades' Association -p.125\n\nMarriage -p.126\n\nObituary -p.126\n\nIndex -p.129\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nMister Brownrigg’s Boys: Magdalen College School and the Great War\n£15.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre XI\n£4.99 Add to cart\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre V\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
